@page "/insights"

<div class="container mt-4">
    <div class="text-center mb-4">
        <h2>🔍 AI-Powered Dish Insights</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">Get data-driven suggestions to maximize flavor and profits.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-green-400 gap-xxl-4">  Tailwind Test</div>

    <div class="alert alert-info mb-4" role="alert">
        <strong>What do <span style="font-size:1.2em;">💬</span> Average Sentiment Score and <span class="text-warning" style="font-size:1.2em;">★</span> Average Rating mean?</strong><br />
        <b>Average Sentiment Score</b> reflects how positively or negatively customers feel about a dish, based on their reviews.
        <ul class="mb-1 mt-2">
            <li><b>Range:</b> 0 (very negative) to 1 (very positive)</li>
            <li><b>0.0 – 0.4:</b> Mostly negative feedback <span style="font-size:1.1em;">😠</span></li>
            <li><b>0.4 – 0.75:</b> Mixed or neutral feedback <span style="font-size:1.1em;">😐</span></li>
            <li><b>0.75 – 1.0:</b> Mostly positive feedback <span style="font-size:1.1em;">😊</span></li>
        </ul>
        <b>Average Rating</b> (<span class="text-warning" style="font-size:1.2em;">★</span>) is the direct score given by customers (1–5 stars).
        <hr class="my-2" />
        <b>How to use these together:</b>
        <ul class="mb-1">
            <li>
                <b>High Sentiment & High Rating:</b> These dishes are loved by customers. Promote them to boost sales and profits.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>High Rating but Low Sentiment:</b> Customers rate the dish well but may have concerns in their comments. Review feedback to improve customer experience and satisfaction.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Low Rating & Low Sentiment:</b> These dishes need attention. Consider recipe changes, presentation, or service improvements to increase satisfaction and profitability.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <span class="text-primary">Combining both metrics helps you identify not just what sells, but what truly delights your customers—leading to better experiences and higher profits.</span>
    </div>

    @if (isloading)
    {
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-center my-5">
            <div class="spinner-border" role="status" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <span class="ms-2 align-self-center">Loading recommendations page...</span>
        </div>
    }
    else if (recommendations == null)
    {
       <div class="alert alert-warning text-center">
        🎉 No recommendations available at this time. Please try again later. 🔁
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h4 class="card-title">🏆 Top Dish Recommendations</h4>
                <p class="card-text">These selections are curated from recent sales trends and review sentiments:</p>
                <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
                    @foreach (var dish in recommendations)
                    {
                        <li class="list-group-item">
                            <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-md-row justify-content-between align-items-md-center">
                                <div>
                                    <span class="fw-bold">🍽️ @dish.RecommendedDish</span>
                                    <div class="mb-1 text-muted small">
                                        Average Rating:
                                        <span class="text-warning" title="Average Rating">
                                            @for (int i = 0; i < Math.Round(dish.AverageRating); i++)
                                            {
                                                <span>★</span>
                                            }
                                            @for (int i = (int)Math.Round(dish.AverageRating); i < 5; i++)
                                            {
                                                <span class="text-secondary">☆</span>
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                            <span class="ms-1">(@dish.AverageRating.ToString("0.0")/5)</span>

                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-2 mt-md-0">
                                    <span title="Average Sentiment Score" class="text-success">
                                        <span style="font-size:1.2em;">💬</span><strong> @dish.AverageSentimentScore.ToString("F2")</strong>
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <div class="card-footer text-muted">
                            <strong>📌 Strategy Note:</strong> @dish.StrategyNote
                        </div>
                    }
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</div>
